okf_version: "1.0"
task: "Check that the ciel MCP session tools (compact) work in Claude Code, Codex and app-server sessions; add compact/new-session where missing; deliver messages in app-server mode over the protocol instead of ConPTY, after surveying every injection endpoint."
reported: "User, 2026-10-01: 'codex나 claude에서 런타임들은 직접적으로 compact를 수행하거나 새로운세션을 여는것을 사용할수없어서 ciel runtime compact를 실행할수있는 mcp를제공히고있는데 이게 claude/codex/app server등에서 잘동작하는지확인하고, 없으면 compact, new session을 지원할수있도록한다. 또, app server모드에서는 메시지 전달이 conty 보다는 리모트 혹은원격으로 전달하는기능을 선호...모든 엔드포인트에 대한 조사후 구현이 필요'. Choices: scope = existing codex-app-server + codex-desktop AND a new Codex TUI --remote mode; new session in terminal runtimes = slash command."
survey_before_change:
  entry_points: "All inputs (POST /ca/chat/messages|notify, Web Chat UI, MCP submit_input, webhooks/SSE receivers, OTLP notices, restart notices) go through RuntimeInputGateway into the runtime-input queue; transports session_socket (Claude only), tty (ConPTY / console-input / POSIX PTY), router (appended to the next model request), and Codex desktop JSON-RPC."
  compact_session: "MCP tool queued a single-slot request file; only the terminal proxies (Claude, Codex TUI, AGY, Muse) consumed it by typing /compact. codex-app-server (bare) and codex-desktop never consumed it. No new-session tool existed (restart_session resume=false relaunched the CLI)."
  bare_app_server: "codex-app-server ran the server only; no channel delivery at all."
  desktop: "codex_desktop_injection delivered over turn/start / turn/steer; thread/compact/start and thread/inject_items existed in the client but were unused."
protocol_experiments (WSL, codex 0.159.3, stub upstream, scratchpad remote_tui_lifecycle_exp*.py):
  - "TUI `codex --remote URL resume <id>` of a thread another client started without turns fails: 'thread/resume failed: no rollout found' -> the TUI must start its own thread."
  - "Every client receives thread/started for threads any client starts (TUI main thread: ephemeral=false, threadSource=user; title threads: ephemeral=true, threadSource=thread_title), but turn notifications only for threads it started or resumed."
  - "turn/start into a thread this client never resumed works and shows in the TUI."
  - "thread/compact/start from a second client runs a compaction turn (upstream got the 'CONTEXT CHECKPOINT COMPACTION' request; TUI shows 'Context compacted')."
  - "TUI /new -> thread/started for the new thread reaches the other client."
changes:
  session_commands: "channel_compact_request_repository: request carries action compact|new_session (missing action = compact). MCP tool new_session added; compact_session description made runtime-neutral; queue_compact takes an action."
  terminal: "channel_compact_injection maps action+runtime: compact -> /compact; new_session -> /clear (claude), /new (codex); unknown runtime leaves the request (deferred, expires by TTL). Proxies take session_command_runtime/session_command_actions (dispatch, terminal context wrappers, Windows and POSIX proxies); Claude and Codex launches pass their runtime."
  app_server_client: "codex_desktop_injection.CodexAppServerChannelInjector (CodexDesktopChannelInjector kept as alias): follows user threads from thread/started, tracks busy/active turns per thread (the client's single global state was overwritten by title-thread notifications), subscribes with thread/resume (retried, deferral logged once), settles turns finished before subscribing via thread/turns/list, executes compact via thread/compact/start (waits for idle) and new_session via thread/start."
  sessions: "new codex_app_server_session.py: CodexBareAppServerSession (bare app-server + channel client when ws://), CodexRemoteTuiSession (runtime codex-remote: server -> channel client -> `codex <same -c overrides> --remote URL` through the terminal proxy with message injection off and only new_session typed; restart re-attaches with resume <followed thread>). run_codex_app_server takes display_name/launch_mode from the session and passes run_server."
  cli: "positional codex-remote / launch-codex-remote, --ca-runtime codex-remote, `last` memory (launch mode codex-remote-router), usage text."
  receipt_fix: "submission_receipt.LatestTranscriptSubmissionReceipt: re-resolves the newest transcript on every check; a transcript first seen after typing is read from its start, accepting only records stamped at/after typing (2 s slack). Found by E2E: first message of a fresh Codex session (transcript_missing) and first after /new were shown in the TUI yet recorded failed prompt_not_submitted."
  ciel_runtime_py: "4980/4980 lines (changed existing lines only)."
e2e (Windows, isolated: scratch CIEL_RUNTIME_CONFIG_DIR, unique router and app-server ports, provider vllm -> local stub upstream, every CIEL_RUNTIME_/ANTHROPIC_/CLAUDE_/CODEX_/OPENAI_ var cleared; scratchpad e2e_rc.py; screenshots by PrintWindow):
  claude: "Claude Code 2.1.286. ALPHA/BETA via session_socket. compact_session -> channel_compact_request_injected command=/compact, screen 'Compacted'. new_session -> command=/clear, new transcript b8a74e6b... created; GAMMA only in the new transcript, ALPHA only in the old one. (e2e-claude-1790847488/shots)"
  codex_tui: "Codex 0.159.3 TUI. compact -> /compact, screen 'Context compacted'. new_session -> /new, GAMMA in the new conversation. Before the receipt fix messages 1 and 3 ended failed prompt_not_submitted although shown; after the fix all three submitted -> replied (e2e-codex-1790847986)."
  codex_remote: "app-server ready -> channel client ready -> TUI started -> target via thread/started. ALPHA/BETA via turn/start; compact via thread/compact/start (screen 'Context compacted'); new_session typed /new, client retargeted via thread/started, GAMMA via turn/start into the new thread; after the reconcile fix all three replied (e2e-codex-remote-1790848344)."
  codex_app_server_bare: "Channel client started its own thread; ALPHA replied there. A separate WebSocket client (playing the person's client) started a thread -> channel client followed and subscribed; the client saw BETA as a userMessage in its thread, then a contextCompaction item from compact_session, then thread/started for the new_session thread; GAMMA went there; all replied (e2e-codex-app-server-*/user-client.jsonl)."
  codex_desktop: "Protocol side: message, compact (thread/compact/start), new_session (thread/start), message into the new thread, all replied. The desktop UI itself did not start: dialog 'ChatGPT failed to start. The process has no package identity.' (OpenAI.Codex 26.924.2738.0 launched by its exe path). Not caused by this change; not fixed."
  cleanup: "Test windows closed by unique title, desktop test instance killed by pid after checking its command line (scratch user-data-dir); copied auth.json removed from scratch; no e2e processes left; live router 9611 healthy."
tests: "Final WSL run (copy of the working tree, CIEL_RUNTIME_* unset, groups sequential): unit 1695 OK (skipped=55), router 1158 OK, channel 442 OK (skipped=80), runtime 343 OK (skipped=19). Targeted: test_codex_desktop_injection (19), test_codex_app_server_session (9), test_channel_compact_injection, test_channel_mcp_tools, test_submission_receipt, test_architecture_contracts (219 passed). ruff clean."
observations_not_changed:
  - "Slash commands other than Claude's /compact are not recorded as user records, so the submit check never confirms them and Enter is pressed up to 4 times (channel_input_submit_unconfirmed attempts=4). The command took effect on the first Enter in every run; the extra Enters hit an empty composer. Same behavior as /compact before this change."
  - "Default app-server listen port (router port + 20) failed to bind once with os error 10013 (65390); the cause was not confirmed (not in the listed excluded ranges). E2E set CIEL_RUNTIME_CODEX_APP_SERVER_LISTEN."
  - "Channel test group exited 1 once from a temp-dir cleanup race when the four groups ran in parallel; alone it passed twice."
not_done:
  - "No prelaunch menu entry for codex-remote (CLI only)."
  - "Codex desktop UI launch failure (package identity) not investigated."
  - "Not committed or pushed."
